# PHASES 1–4 — Capabilities

## Invariants for every phase

1. **Existing exports frozen.** No signature change, no new required field, no changed default. New optional fields only, where `undefined` reproduces today's behaviour exactly.
2. **Zero new runtime dependencies.** Everything builds on `langchain`, `@langchain/core`, `@langchain/langgraph`, `zod`. If a phase seems to need one, stop and escalate.
3. **No LangChain type crosses the public boundary.** `BaseLanguageModel`, `AgentMiddleware`, `BaseCheckpointSaver`, `BaseStore` must not appear in any exported signature. This is what makes the *next* upgrade a non-event for consumers.
4. **New code in new files.** Existing files gain only a dispatch branch guarded by a new optional field.
5. **Per-phase regression file** — `test/regression/no-delta-<phase>.test.ts` — constructs an agent with today's config and asserts composed middleware array, bound tool names, and system prompt are unchanged. This is the enforcement mechanism, not optional.
6. **No test calls a real provider.** Stub the model; assert what the wrapper passed to LangChain, not what LangChain did with it.

## Public surface delta (entire consumer-visible addition)

```ts
interface AgentConfig {
  // ...everything existing, untouched...
  profile?: 'react' | 'deep';                    // default 'react'
  planning?: boolean | { systemPrompt?: string; toolDescription?: string };
  filesystem?: FilesystemSpec;
  subagents?: SubagentSpec[];
  contextManagement?: boolean | { triggerTokens?: number; keepRecentMessages?: number };
}

type FilesystemSpec =
  | 'state' | { kind: 'state' }
  | { kind: 'store'; namespace?: string[] }
  | { kind: 'node'; root: string; readOnly?: boolean };

interface SubagentSpec {
  name: string;
  description: string;          // what the parent model sees when choosing
  systemPrompt: string;
  model?: ModelSpec;            // defaults to parent's
  tools?: ToolSpec[];           // defaults to parent's, minus `task`
  filesystem?: 'inherit' | 'isolated' | false;
}

class AgentConfigError extends Error {}  // TOOL_NAME_COLLISION | UNKNOWN_BACKEND | SUBAGENT_DEPTH_EXCEEDED | ...
```

